1
00:02:32,097 --> 00:02:33,981
<v Woman> Gina speaking. How can I help you?

2
00:02:33,981 --> 00:02:37,056
<v Man> Oh, hello - I'd like to order some stationery, please.

3
00:02:37,056 --> 00:02:39,037
<v Woman> And who am I speaking to?

4
00:02:39,037 --> 00:02:40,422
<v Man> John Carter.

5
00:02:40,422 --> 00:02:45,784
<v Woman> Right - can I just confirm your account number and the name of your company, John?

6
00:02:45,784 --> 00:02:50,282
<v Man> Sure! The account number is 6 9 2 4 double 1

7
00:02:50,282 --> 00:02:57,416
<v Woman> Six nine two four one one. Right, and you're from 'Rainbow Computers?'

8
00:02:57,416 --> 00:03:01,056
<v Man> No. The company is Rainbow Communications

9
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:10,084
<v Woman> Oh, OK, I'll just fix that on the system ... communications. And what would you like to order, John?

10
00:03:10,084 --> 00:03:15,203
<v Man> Envelopes. We need a box of A4 - that is, normal size envelopes

11
00:03:15,203 --> 00:03:17,545
<v Woman> White, yellow or vanilla?

12
00:03:17,545 --> 00:03:22,166
<v Man> We'll have the plain white please - but the ones with the little windows

13
00:03:22,166 --> 00:03:29,218
<v Woman> OK ... One box - A4 - white - just the one box, was it?

14
00:03:29,218 --> 00:03:38,840
<v Man> Um, on second thoughts make that two boxes. We go through heaps of envelopes. As a matter of interest. Are they made from recycled paper?

15
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:46,062
<v Woman> No. You can't get white recycled paper. The recycled ones are grey and they're more expensive actually.

16
00:03:46,062 --> 00:03:48,298
<v Man> Right - we'll stick to white then.

17
00:03:48,298 --> 00:03:50,171
<v Woman> Something else, John?

18
00:03:50,171 --> 00:03:54,705
<v Man> Yes, we need some coloured photocopy paper. What colours do you have?

19
00:03:54,705 --> 00:04:03,639
<v Woman> We've got purple, light blue, blue, light green - whatever you want, pretty much. There are 500 sheets to the pack.

20
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:13,864
<v Man> Let's see ...we're going to need a lot of blue paper for our new price lists so can you give us ten packs, please. Make sure it's the light blue though...

21
00:04:13,864 --> 00:04:16,332
<v Woman> Ten packs of the light blue.

22
00:04:49,931 --> 00:04:51,345
<v Woman> Anything else that we can help you with?

23
00:04:51,345 --> 00:04:57,491
<v Man> Let me think ... what else do we need? I'm sure there was something else.

24
00:04:57,491 --> 00:05:03,064
<v Woman> Pens, paper clips, fax paper, computer supplies, office furniture?

25
00:05:03,064 --> 00:05:07,432
<v Man> Oh, yes! We need floppy disks - do you have those nice coloured ones?

26
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:10,922
<v Woman> Yes, but they're a bit more expensive than the black ones.

27
00:05:10,922 --> 00:05:13,195
<v Man> That's alright. I'm not paying, anyway!

28
00:05:13,195 --> 00:05:23,779
<v Woman> Right. Floppy disks. And what about diaries for next year? We've got them in stock already and it's a good idea to order early.

29
00:05:23,779 --> 00:05:34,187
<v Man> No - I think we're alright for diaries but something we do need is one of those big wall calendars - you know, one that shows the whole year at a glance. Do you stock those?

30
00:05:34,187 --> 00:05:35,502
<v Woman> We certainly do.

31
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:42,752
<v Man> OK - can you include a wall calendar then, with the other stuff. Just make sure it's got the whole year on the one side.

32
00:05:42,752 --> 00:05:45,939
<v Woman> Sure - and do you have a copy of our new catalogue?

33
00:05:45,939 --> 00:05:48,044
<v Man> No, I don't, but could you send one.

34
00:05:48,044 --> 00:05:55,847
<v Woman> Yes! I'll pop one in with the order. You'll find it a lot easier to remember what you need if you have our catalogue in front of you next time.

35
00:05:55,847 --> 00:06:00,144
<v Man> Yes, good idea. And when can you deliver this?

36
00:06:00,144 --> 00:06:02,168
<v Woman> Should be with you tomorrow morning.

37
00:06:02,168 --> 00:06:09,013
<v Man> Can you make sure that it's not after 11.30am because I have to go out at 12 there's only myself here on Fridays.

38
00:06:09,013 --> 00:06:15,541
<v Woman> Fine - I'll make a note on the delivery docket that they should deliver before half past eleven. Thanks very much.

39
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:16,422
<v Man> Thanks.